WEBVTT

00:00:00.351 --> 00:00:01.492
About the Author.

00:00:01.512 --> 00:00:17.608
Mark Twain was born in Florida, Missouri, in 1835.

00:00:17.668 --> 00:00:33.180
His real name was Samuel Langhorn Clemens.

00:00:33.240 --> 00:00:39.792
When he was a boy, he lived in Hannibal, Missouri, on the Mississippi River.

00:00:39.852 --> 00:00:45.763
Many of the adventures in his books are about his youth in Hannibal.

00:00:45.823 --> 00:00:52.735
In 1857, he worked as a pilot on a steamboat on the Mississippi River.

00:00:52.794 --> 00:00:58.774
In 1861, he went to California and his life changed there.

00:00:58.834 --> 00:01:05.469
He began writing stories for a San Francisco newspaper called The Morning Call.

00:01:05.528 --> 00:01:14.957
At this time, he changed his real name, Samuel Clemens, to a pen name, Mark Twain.

00:01:15.017 --> 00:01:22.454
In 1867, he published his short story, The Celebrated Jumping Frog of Calaveras County.

00:01:22.514 --> 00:01:27.095
It was a big success, and he became famous.

00:01:27.154 --> 00:01:31.483
He traveled to Hawaii and Europe.

00:01:31.543 --> 00:01:42.338
In 1870, Mark Twain married Olivia Levy Langdon, and they had three daughters, Susan, Jean and Clara.

00:01:42.398 --> 00:01:47.070
He and his family lived happily in Hartford, Connecticut.

00:01:47.130 --> 00:02:04.690
Here, he wrote his three great books, The Adventures of Tom Sawyer, 1876, Life on the Mississippi, 1883, and The Adventures of Huckleberry Finn, 1884.

00:02:04.750 --> 00:02:09.002
People everywhere liked his books.

00:02:09.062 --> 00:02:17.946
Later in his life Mark Twain had financial problems, and he and his family moved to Europe for nine years.

00:02:18.006 --> 00:02:24.596
When his daughters Susie and Jean died, he became a very unhappy man.

00:02:24.656 --> 00:02:30.826
He loved his wife very much and she died too in 1904.

00:02:30.886 --> 00:02:37.999
After her death, he went to live in New York City and then in Reading, Connecticut.

00:02:38.059 --> 00:02:42.581
He died in 1910 at the age of 75.

00:02:42.641 --> 00:02:59.926
His other works include The Prince and the Popper, 1881, The Innocence Abroad, 1869, A Connecticut Yankee in King Arthur's Court, 1889, and many short stories.

00:02:59.986 --> 00:03:12.604
He was the first American writer to change the American way of writing with his simple and funny language.

00:03:12.664 --> 00:03:23.781
In 1537, two boys were born on the same day in London.

00:03:23.841 --> 00:03:29.115
Tom Canty was born to a poor family of porpers.

00:03:29.175 --> 00:03:36.770
They lived in one room near Pudding Lane, a poor neighborhood near London Bridge.

00:03:36.830 --> 00:03:39.442
Another child.

00:03:39.502 --> 00:03:43.566
Said Tom's father when he saw the baby.

00:03:43.626 --> 00:03:46.718
Another mouth to feed.

00:03:46.778 --> 00:03:49.430
He was not happy.

00:03:49.490 --> 00:03:52.533
No one wanted Tom.

00:03:52.593 --> 00:03:58.648
The other baby was Edward Tudor, Prince of Wales.

00:03:58.708 --> 00:04:03.783
His father was Henry VIII, King of England.

00:04:03.843 --> 00:04:07.877
They lived at Westminster Palace.

00:04:07.937 --> 00:04:10.790
A prince is born!

00:04:10.850 --> 00:04:13.622
And some prince is born!

00:04:13.682 --> 00:04:17.894
cried everyone at Westminster Palace.

00:04:17.954 --> 00:04:25.475
Let's have a big celebration with fireworks and a banquet.

00:04:25.535 --> 00:04:28.456
My son is born.

00:04:28.516 --> 00:04:31.587
Said the king happily.

00:04:31.647 --> 00:04:38.828
All of England was happy and celebrated the arrival of the baby prince.

00:04:38.888 --> 00:04:45.942
13 years later, Tom was begging for money on the streets of London.

00:04:46.001 --> 00:04:52.286
His clothes were old and full of holes, and he had no shoes.

00:04:52.346 --> 00:04:55.648
He was thin and dirty.

00:04:55.708 --> 00:05:03.785
He lived with his mother, grandmother and two sisters, Bette and Nan.

00:05:03.844 --> 00:05:09.554
The children had no beds and slept on the cold floor.

00:05:09.614 --> 00:05:13.160
They were always hungry.

00:05:13.220 --> 00:05:18.912
Tom's father, John Canty, never did any work.

00:05:18.972 --> 00:05:24.193
He sent Tom out to beg every day of the year.

00:05:24.253 --> 00:05:30.475
Sometimes people felt sorry for Tom and gave him a little money.

00:05:30.534 --> 00:05:35.386
But other times, he did not get anything.

00:05:35.446 --> 00:05:42.222
When he did not bring any money home, His father hit him.

00:05:42.282 --> 00:05:49.388
I don't want to always be poor, thought Tom.

00:05:49.448 --> 00:05:57.794
I want to learn to read and write, and I want to know about the world.

00:05:57.854 --> 00:06:04.038
Father Andrew was a kind old priest with white hair.

00:06:04.098 --> 00:06:09.931
He was Tom's friend and lived in the same building.

00:06:09.991 --> 00:06:14.182
Can you help me, Father Andrew?"

00:06:14.242 --> 00:06:16.365
Tom asked.

00:06:16.425 --> 00:06:27.106
I want to read and write, and I want to speak good English, like princes and important people.

00:06:27.166 --> 00:06:30.269
I can help you, Tom.

00:06:30.329 --> 00:06:32.582
Said Father Andrew.

00:06:32.641 --> 00:06:36.191
Come to my room every day.

00:06:36.251 --> 00:06:42.562
He taught Tom to read and write, and he taught him Latin.

00:06:42.621 --> 00:06:47.286
He told him stories about kings and princes.

00:06:47.346 --> 00:06:53.100
Tom learned quickly and soon read Father Andrew's books.

00:06:53.160 --> 00:06:59.164
At night, he often dreamed about the people in those books.

00:06:59.224 --> 00:07:05.404
When Tom was with other boys, he liked playing at being a prince.

00:07:05.464 --> 00:07:12.844
The other boys laughed at him and called him Prince Tom, but they liked him.

00:07:12.904 --> 00:07:17.778
They jumped in the mud and swam in the river.

00:07:17.838 --> 00:07:28.004
One day, Father Andrew said, Tom, why don't you go to Westminster Palace and see the real Prince?

00:07:28.064 --> 00:07:31.296
Prince Edward is the king's son.

00:07:31.356 --> 00:07:36.147
Perhaps you can see him at the palace.

00:07:36.207 --> 00:07:43.661
Chapter 2 The pauper meets the prince.

00:07:43.721 --> 00:07:52.249
The next morning Tom went to Westminster Palace and stood outside the big gate.

00:07:52.308 --> 00:07:56.002
There were two tall soldiers there.

00:07:56.062 --> 00:08:02.264
He looked at the splendid palace, but he could not go near it.

00:08:02.324 --> 00:08:13.060
He went back the next day and saw important ladies and gentlemen going to the palace, but he never saw the prince.

00:08:13.120 --> 00:08:22.178
Then one day he went back there again and saw a boy in very fine clothes.

00:08:22.238 --> 00:08:25.660
That looks like the prince!

00:08:25.720 --> 00:08:30.556
Thought Tom excitedly, he ran to the gate.

00:08:30.616 --> 00:08:33.398
You can't come in here.

00:08:33.418 --> 00:08:37.972
The soldiers cried and hit Tom.

00:08:38.032 --> 00:08:42.744
The prince saw this and did not like it.

00:08:42.804 --> 00:08:45.716
Why did you hit the poor boy?

00:08:45.776 --> 00:08:47.528
Asked Edward.

00:08:47.588 --> 00:08:50.680
Open the gates and bring him in.

00:08:50.740 --> 00:08:51.980
But sir.

00:08:52.040 --> 00:08:53.351
Said the soldier.

00:08:53.411 --> 00:08:55.983
He's only a dirty beggar.

00:08:56.042 --> 00:09:00.856
My father is the king of rich people and poor people.

00:09:00.916 --> 00:09:03.008
answered Edward.

00:09:03.068 --> 00:09:08.052
The soldiers opened the gate and brought Tom in.

00:09:08.112 --> 00:09:10.182
Come with me!

00:09:10.242 --> 00:09:12.584
Edward said kindly.

00:09:12.644 --> 00:09:20.198
He took Tom inside the big palace with its long stairs and beautiful rooms.

00:09:20.258 --> 00:09:25.440
When they reached the prince's rooms, Edward called a servant.

00:09:25.500 --> 00:09:28.488
Bring food, he ordered.

00:09:28.548 --> 00:09:31.858
Meat, bread and fruit.

00:09:31.918 --> 00:09:37.399
Tom was very hungry, and he ate the food quickly.

00:09:37.459 --> 00:09:41.300
Now, said the prince, smiling.

00:09:41.360 --> 00:09:43.250
What's your name?

00:09:43.310 --> 00:09:45.670
Where do you live?

00:09:45.730 --> 00:09:53.233
My name's Tom Canty, and I live with my family in a room near Pudding Lane.

00:09:53.294 --> 00:09:55.316
In one room?

00:09:55.376 --> 00:09:56.866
said the prince.

00:09:56.926 --> 00:10:00.107
Do you all live in one room?

00:10:00.167 --> 00:10:03.088
Yes, said Tom.

00:10:03.148 --> 00:10:07.739
There are hundreds of rooms here, said the prince.

00:10:07.799 --> 00:10:10.440
I have five rooms.

00:10:10.500 --> 00:10:14.770
We're very poor, said Tom.

00:10:14.830 --> 00:10:20.045
My father doesn't work, and I have to beg for money.

00:10:20.105 --> 00:10:24.400
When I don't bring money home, he hits me.

00:10:24.460 --> 00:10:27.310
Oh, your father hits you.

00:10:27.370 --> 00:10:28.741
Said the prince.

00:10:28.801 --> 00:10:33.933
I'll send my soldiers to your house, and they'll put him in prison.

00:10:33.993 --> 00:10:36.634
No, no, please sir.

00:10:36.694 --> 00:10:37.984
Said Tom.

00:10:38.044 --> 00:10:41.426
Think of my mother and sisters.

00:10:41.486 --> 00:10:43.566
I understand.

00:10:43.626 --> 00:10:46.087
Said the prince kindly.

00:10:46.147 --> 00:10:48.492
I have two sisters.

00:10:48.552 --> 00:10:51.836
Lady Elizabeth and Lady Mary.

00:10:51.896 --> 00:10:57.788
Lady Elizabeth is very nice, but I don't like Lady Mary.

00:10:57.848 --> 00:11:01.230
She never laughs or smiles.

00:11:01.290 --> 00:11:06.032
I also have a cousin, Lady Jane Grey.

00:11:06.092 --> 00:11:09.614
She's my age and is very kind.

00:11:09.674 --> 00:11:12.894
But I don't know any boys.

00:11:12.954 --> 00:11:15.586
Do you play with other boys?

00:11:15.646 --> 00:11:19.304
Of course I do, said Tom.

00:11:19.364 --> 00:11:21.011
I don't.

00:11:21.071 --> 00:11:23.882
Said the prince, sadly.

00:11:23.942 --> 00:11:26.104
What do you play?

00:11:26.164 --> 00:11:30.998
We play by the river, swim and jump in the mud.

00:11:31.058 --> 00:11:32.829
Said Tom.

00:11:32.888 --> 00:11:39.974
Sometimes we play princes and soldiers and other times we play ball.

00:11:40.034 --> 00:11:44.497
We dance and sing and make a lot of noise too.

00:11:44.557 --> 00:11:47.774
We always have great fun.

00:11:47.834 --> 00:11:54.452
I want to play by the river and swim and jump in the mud once in my life.

00:11:54.512 --> 00:11:58.184
But I can't, because I'm a prince.

00:11:58.244 --> 00:12:00.906
Said Edward, sadly.

00:12:00.966 --> 00:12:06.050
He looked out of the window and then said suddenly.

00:12:06.110 --> 00:12:07.942
I've got an idea.

00:12:08.002 --> 00:12:10.013
Look in the mirror.

00:12:10.073 --> 00:12:12.594
You and I are the same.

00:12:12.654 --> 00:12:16.572
You're like me and I'm like you.

00:12:16.632 --> 00:12:19.810
The two boys were both thin.

00:12:19.870 --> 00:12:30.829
They had the same brown hair, the same brown eyes, the same nose, the same mouth and the same voice.

00:12:30.890 --> 00:12:33.912
They were also the same height.

00:12:33.972 --> 00:12:37.196
They were almost identical.

00:12:37.256 --> 00:12:39.808
The prince was excited.

00:12:39.868 --> 00:12:42.164
Let's change clothes.

00:12:42.224 --> 00:12:47.149
You'll be the prince and I'll be the pauper for a short time.

00:12:47.209 --> 00:12:48.479
It'll be a game.

00:12:48.499 --> 00:12:51.220
A wonderful game.

00:12:51.280 --> 00:12:55.901
Take off those old clothes and put on my clothes.

00:12:55.961 --> 00:12:59.952
We can both be happy for a short time.

00:13:00.012 --> 00:13:06.104
Tom washed his face and put on the prince's elegant clothes.

00:13:06.164 --> 00:13:11.536
Then Edward put on Tom's dirty old trousers and shirt.

00:13:11.596 --> 00:13:16.402
Now Edward was Tom, and Tom was Edward.

00:13:16.462 --> 00:13:22.818
They looked at each other in the big mirror and laughed loudly.

00:13:22.878 --> 00:13:28.664
Stay here until I come back, said the prince happily.

00:13:28.724 --> 00:13:32.176
I want to be a pauper for an hour.

00:13:32.236 --> 00:13:38.349
I'm going to swim in the river and jump in the mud with the other boys.

00:13:38.409 --> 00:13:44.268
before leaving, he took something big and round from the table.

00:13:44.328 --> 00:13:51.602
He went to a corner of the room and put it inside an old Italian suit of armor.

00:13:51.662 --> 00:13:55.103
Then he ran out of the door.

00:13:55.164 --> 00:13:57.984
But what will I do?

00:13:58.044 --> 00:14:01.936
Tom asked himself.

00:14:01.996 --> 00:14:12.850
Chapter 3 Changing Places The prince went to the gates of the palace.

00:14:12.910 --> 00:14:16.022
Open the palace gates quickly!

00:14:16.082 --> 00:14:17.834
He ordered.

00:14:17.894 --> 00:14:23.268
The soldiers opened the gates and Edward went out.

00:14:23.328 --> 00:14:27.240
One of the soldiers hit him on the head.

00:14:27.300 --> 00:14:32.318
Don't give orders to the king's soldiers, boy.

00:14:32.378 --> 00:14:40.175
Edward fell to the ground and said, I'm Prince Edward, Prince of Wales.

00:14:40.235 --> 00:14:43.757
Well, then I'm the King of England.

00:14:43.816 --> 00:14:46.848
Said the soldier laughing.

00:14:46.908 --> 00:14:50.009
You can go to prison for that.

00:14:50.069 --> 00:14:52.720
Said Edward angrily.

00:14:52.780 --> 00:14:55.071
His face was red.

00:14:55.131 --> 00:15:01.938
The crowd laughed loudly and said, He's mad!

00:15:01.998 --> 00:15:07.235
Edward walked down the road angrily.

00:15:07.295 --> 00:15:14.118
He forgot about playing by the river and walked in the streets of London.

00:15:14.178 --> 00:15:18.279
This was his first walk in the city.

00:15:18.339 --> 00:15:22.410
He was soon lost and tired.

00:15:22.470 --> 00:15:31.541
His feet hurt a lot because he had no shoes and his stomach hurt because he was hungry.

00:15:31.602 --> 00:15:36.602
I must go back to the palace," he thought.

00:15:36.662 --> 00:15:43.257
He stopped people and said, show me the way to Westminster Palace.

00:15:43.318 --> 00:15:48.902
He never said, please, because he was the prince.

00:15:48.962 --> 00:15:56.596
Some people laughed at him, and others were angry because he was not polite.

00:15:56.656 --> 00:15:59.942
But no one helped him.

00:16:00.002 --> 00:16:03.838
This is terrible, he thought.

00:16:03.898 --> 00:16:09.999
I'm hungry and cold, and I don't know where to sleep tonight.

00:16:10.059 --> 00:16:13.129
Tom's house is near Pudding Lane.

00:16:13.189 --> 00:16:17.560
Perhaps Tom's mother and sisters will help me.

00:16:17.620 --> 00:16:23.581
Edward walked for a long time in the dark, dirty streets.

00:16:23.641 --> 00:16:27.370
There was a bad smell everywhere.

00:16:27.430 --> 00:16:32.060
Then it started to rain and it was cold.

00:16:32.120 --> 00:16:34.992
Edward was unhappy.

00:16:35.052 --> 00:16:41.114
Suddenly, he felt a big, heavy hand around his arm.

00:16:41.174 --> 00:16:46.938
What are you doing out at this time, Tom Canty?

00:16:46.998 --> 00:16:49.709
Asked a big man.

00:16:49.770 --> 00:16:53.772
Where's the money from your day's work?

00:16:53.832 --> 00:16:55.042
Ouch!

00:16:55.102 --> 00:16:56.850
You're hurting me!

00:16:56.911 --> 00:16:58.868
cried Edward.

00:16:58.928 --> 00:17:00.929
Are you his father?

00:17:00.949 --> 00:17:03.190
His father.

00:17:03.250 --> 00:17:06.902
I'm your father, you stupid boy.

00:17:06.962 --> 00:17:10.673
Said John Canty, hitting Edward.

00:17:10.734 --> 00:17:12.394
No!

00:17:12.414 --> 00:17:12.884
No!

00:17:12.944 --> 00:17:15.005
cried Edward.

00:17:15.065 --> 00:17:19.026
I'm Edward, the Prince of Wales.

00:17:19.087 --> 00:17:22.576
Your son is in Westminster Palace.

00:17:22.637 --> 00:17:27.826
He's wearing my clothes and I'm wearing his clothes.

00:17:27.886 --> 00:17:30.207
We changed places.

00:17:30.267 --> 00:17:32.298
It was a game.

00:17:32.358 --> 00:17:35.158
Take me to the palace.

00:17:35.218 --> 00:17:42.980
John Canty looked at the boy with cold eyes and said, You're mad.

00:17:43.040 --> 00:17:44.601
Mad.

00:17:44.661 --> 00:17:49.932
He took Edward's arm and pulled him down the road.

00:17:49.992 --> 00:17:52.697
You're coming home with me.

00:17:52.757 --> 00:18:00.246
And tomorrow morning you can start work early and bring some money home.

00:18:00.306 --> 00:18:06.068
At the palace, Tom was alone in the prince's room.

00:18:06.128 --> 00:18:13.944
He looked at himself in the big mirror on the wall and liked his new clothes.

00:18:14.004 --> 00:18:18.902
He looked at all the beautiful things around him.

00:18:18.962 --> 00:18:33.970
pictures of kings, queens, princes and princesses, lovely chairs and tables, beautiful glasses and cups, and big plates full of fruit.

00:18:34.030 --> 00:18:39.174
He touched the prince's sword and played with it for a while.

00:18:39.234 --> 00:18:45.298
He was happy in the prince's room and liked playing this new game.

00:18:45.358 --> 00:18:49.670
But after an hour, he was tired of it.

00:18:49.730 --> 00:18:53.102
And he began to feel afraid.

00:18:53.162 --> 00:18:56.733
Where is the real prince?

00:18:56.794 --> 00:18:58.514
He thought.

00:18:58.575 --> 00:19:01.116
Why isn't he back?

00:19:01.176 --> 00:19:04.228
I must look for him.

00:19:04.288 --> 00:19:09.552
He opened a big door and saw four gentlemen.

00:19:09.612 --> 00:19:12.664
They bowed to Tom.

00:19:12.724 --> 00:19:14.381
Oh!

00:19:14.441 --> 00:19:15.979
Right, Tom.

00:19:16.039 --> 00:19:18.230
And shut the door quickly.

00:19:18.290 --> 00:19:20.442
How strange.

00:19:20.502 --> 00:19:22.294
One gentleman said.

00:19:22.354 --> 00:19:25.356
The prince is probably ill.

00:19:25.416 --> 00:19:29.319
Let's call his sisters or Lady Jane.

00:19:29.380 --> 00:19:32.252
Said the second gentleman.

00:19:32.312 --> 00:19:37.905
A beautiful young woman with a kind face opened the door.

00:19:37.966 --> 00:19:41.446
It was Lady Jane Grey.

00:19:41.506 --> 00:19:46.064
Tom was afraid and went down on his knees.

00:19:46.125 --> 00:19:49.706
Please save me, kind lady.

00:19:49.766 --> 00:19:51.556
Said Tom.

00:19:51.616 --> 00:19:54.378
I'm not Prince Edward.

00:19:54.438 --> 00:19:58.950
My name's Tom Canty and I'm a pauper.

00:19:59.010 --> 00:20:02.551
Prince Edward and I change clothes.

00:20:02.611 --> 00:20:09.682
He's wearing my dirty old clothes and I'm wearing his beautiful clothes.

00:20:09.742 --> 00:20:15.492
Please find the prince so I can get my clothes back.

00:20:15.552 --> 00:20:19.512
Oh dear, you're ill Edward.

00:20:19.572 --> 00:20:22.393
Lady Jane said.

00:20:22.453 --> 00:20:25.414
Please come with me.

00:20:25.474 --> 00:20:28.874
Your father wants to see you.

00:20:28.934 --> 00:20:34.015
My father is John Canty here.

00:20:34.075 --> 00:20:36.106
Ask Tom.

00:20:36.166 --> 00:20:40.667
Lady Jane did not answer him.

00:20:40.727 --> 00:20:47.032
The king is very ill, she said sadly.

00:20:47.092 --> 00:20:51.334
Tom followed her to the king's bedroom.

00:20:51.394 --> 00:20:57.248
King Henry was in bed and his face was white.

00:20:57.308 --> 00:21:04.402
Here is your son, your Majesty, said Lady Jane.

00:21:04.462 --> 00:21:09.950
The king opened his eyes and smiled at Tom.

00:21:10.010 --> 00:21:12.976
What's the matter, Edward?

00:21:13.037 --> 00:21:15.237
Tell your father.

00:21:15.297 --> 00:21:17.988
Are you the king?

00:21:18.048 --> 00:21:23.169
Ask Tom, looking at the big fat man.

00:21:23.229 --> 00:21:25.730
Of course I'm the king.

00:21:25.790 --> 00:21:28.710
Don't you know your father?

00:21:28.770 --> 00:21:31.496
Tom bowed.

00:21:31.556 --> 00:21:35.061
Sir, I'm not your son.

00:21:35.081 --> 00:21:37.622
I'm not the prince.

00:21:37.682 --> 00:21:39.763
I'm poor Tom.

00:21:39.783 --> 00:21:44.045
Stop this nonsense, said King Henry.

00:21:44.105 --> 00:21:49.507
You are the prince, and you will be king when I die.

00:21:49.567 --> 00:21:53.949
Now, go and rest before the banquet tonight.

00:21:54.009 --> 00:21:58.165
There'll be a lot of important men.

00:21:58.226 --> 00:22:04.405
Tom and Lady Jane went back to the Prince's room.

00:22:04.465 --> 00:22:10.780
After a short time, Lord Hartford went to see King Henry.

00:22:10.840 --> 00:22:16.774
Lord Hartford was a short, fat man with a long nose.

00:22:16.834 --> 00:22:20.688
He was the king's first Lord.

00:22:20.748 --> 00:22:29.530
Lord Hartford said the king, I'm very ill, but I must continue working.

00:22:29.590 --> 00:22:33.666
I have to read and sign many papers.

00:22:33.726 --> 00:22:36.766
Where is the great seal?

00:22:36.826 --> 00:22:40.527
You gave it to Prince Edward two days ago.

00:22:40.587 --> 00:22:42.908
Said Lord Hartford.

00:22:42.968 --> 00:22:45.848
I'll go and get it.

00:22:45.908 --> 00:22:52.410
Lord Hartford came back without the great seal and he was worried.

00:22:52.470 --> 00:22:54.070
Your Majesty?

00:22:54.130 --> 00:22:55.200
He said.

00:22:55.260 --> 00:23:00.230
The Prince can't remember where it is or what it is.

00:23:00.290 --> 00:23:02.619
He can't remember.

00:23:02.639 --> 00:23:06.062
Then he really is ill.

00:23:06.122 --> 00:23:10.374
The great seal is very important.

00:23:10.434 --> 00:23:14.327
Let's wait until he's better.

00:23:14.387 --> 00:23:20.280
At one o'clock that afternoon, Tom had lunch.

00:23:20.340 --> 00:23:27.710
He was surprised when he saw the royal dining room with its gold furniture.

00:23:27.770 --> 00:23:32.395
Several servants stood near him while he ate.

00:23:32.456 --> 00:23:41.080
Poor Tom made a lot of mistakes that afternoon, but no one laughed because they thought he was ill.

00:23:41.140 --> 00:23:46.452
He ate with his fingers and made noises with his mouth.

00:23:46.512 --> 00:23:51.944
Then he looked at his napkin with great interest.

00:23:52.004 --> 00:23:56.630
Please take this lovely napkin away.

00:23:56.690 --> 00:24:00.885
I don't want to make it dirty.

00:24:00.946 --> 00:24:06.668
Then he took a lot of nuts and put them in his pockets.

00:24:06.729 --> 00:24:12.042
At the end of the meal, a servant brought a finger bowl.

00:24:12.102 --> 00:24:16.144
But Tom did not clean his fingers in it.

00:24:16.204 --> 00:24:20.436
He drank from it.

00:24:20.496 --> 00:24:34.066
King Henry VIII In the story you are reading, King Henry VIII is Prince Edward's father.

00:24:34.126 --> 00:24:41.649
He was one of England's most famous kings and ruled from 1509 to 1547.

00:24:41.709 --> 00:24:46.121
Who was King Henry VIII and what did he do?

00:24:46.141 --> 00:25:01.481
Young Henry Henry VIII was born on the 28th of June 1491.

00:25:01.542 --> 00:25:08.246
He was a tall, good-looking man with red hair and blue eyes.

00:25:08.306 --> 00:25:13.508
He liked playing tennis, hunting and riding horses.

00:25:13.568 --> 00:25:18.162
He also liked reading, music and dancing.

00:25:18.222 --> 00:25:20.664
He was an intelligent man.

00:25:20.724 --> 00:25:27.248
and spoke English, French, Spanish, and Latin.

00:25:27.308 --> 00:25:35.679
Henry became king when he was almost eighteen, and married Catherine of Aragon.

00:25:35.739 --> 00:25:40.450
She was the daughter of King Ferdinand of Spain.

00:25:40.510 --> 00:25:45.647
They were happy together for almost twenty years.

00:25:45.707 --> 00:25:52.086
During Henry's reign, the Renaissance developed in England.

00:25:52.146 --> 00:26:00.380
There were always many writers, poets, painters and musicians at his court.

00:26:00.441 --> 00:26:10.596
The young king lived in beautiful castles and palaces and wore expensive clothes and jewels.

00:26:10.656 --> 00:26:14.330
King Henry wanted a son.

00:26:14.390 --> 00:26:18.054
but Catherine could not give him one.

00:26:18.114 --> 00:26:26.406
During his twenty years of marriage, four sons were born, but they all died.

00:26:26.466 --> 00:26:31.748
Only a daughter called Princess Mary survived.

00:26:31.808 --> 00:26:38.510
The king wanted a son to become king after his death.

00:26:38.570 --> 00:26:43.424
Henry meets Anne Boleyn.

00:26:43.484 --> 00:26:49.320
In 1526 Henry met Anne Berlin.

00:26:49.380 --> 00:26:55.314
She was a young English woman with dark hair and dark eyes.

00:26:55.374 --> 00:27:00.248
Henry fell in love with her and wanted to marry her.

00:27:00.308 --> 00:27:03.190
He wanted a son from her.

00:27:03.250 --> 00:27:12.438
He decided to divorce Catherine, but he was Catholic and he needed permission from the Pope in Rome.

00:27:12.498 --> 00:27:20.914
The Pope did not give him permission, and Henry was very angry.

00:27:20.974 --> 00:27:28.908
In 1533 he chose a new archbishop of Canterbury called Thomas Cranmer.

00:27:28.968 --> 00:27:33.620
Cranmer believed in the complete power of the king.

00:27:33.680 --> 00:27:38.799
Soon he helped to establish the Church of England.

00:27:38.860 --> 00:27:45.940
This church had different rooms and Henry was able to divorce Catherine.

00:27:46.000 --> 00:27:53.102
Henry and Anne Berlin were secretly married and Catherine left the court.

00:27:53.163 --> 00:28:00.636
In May 1533 Anne gave birth to Princess Elizabeth.

00:28:00.696 --> 00:28:06.443
Henry was unhappy with Anne because she did not give him a son.

00:28:06.503 --> 00:28:11.918
However, Princess Elizabeth later became a great queen.

00:28:11.978 --> 00:28:15.640
Queen Elizabeth the first.

00:28:15.700 --> 00:28:24.932
Jane Seymour When Henry met Jane Seymour, he fell in love with her.

00:28:24.992 --> 00:28:34.210
He was a friend of her father, Sir John Seymour of Wiltshire, and met her at her father's house.

00:28:34.270 --> 00:28:38.560
He also thought she could give him a son.

00:28:38.620 --> 00:28:46.455
Henry accused Anne of treason, and she was beheaded in 1536.

00:28:46.515 --> 00:28:56.282
Henry soon married Jane Seymour, and in 1537, Jane gave birth to a son, Prince Edward.

00:28:56.342 --> 00:29:01.666
King Henry was very happy, and everyone in England celebrated.

00:29:01.726 --> 00:29:05.375
The king finally had a son.

00:29:05.436 --> 00:29:12.605
but Queen Jane died 12 days later and Henry was very sad.

00:29:12.665 --> 00:29:19.808
Prince Edward had the best teachers and received an excellent education.

00:29:19.868 --> 00:29:28.690
During this time Henry built beautiful palaces, castles and homes around England.

00:29:28.750 --> 00:29:33.326
One of these was Deal Castle in Kent.

00:29:33.386 --> 00:29:42.708
Henry built many warships, and England soon had the strongest navy in Europe.

00:29:42.768 --> 00:29:51.876
Political problems Spain and France were Henry's enemies.

00:29:51.936 --> 00:30:01.124
He needed a strong ally, so he decided to marry a German princess called Anne of Cleves.

00:30:01.183 --> 00:30:09.518
The royal painter Hans Holbein went to Germany to paint a portrait of Anne of Cleeds.

00:30:09.578 --> 00:30:19.394
Henry liked her portrait, but when she arrived in England he was surprised because she was ugly and didn't speak English.

00:30:19.454 --> 00:30:27.818
Henry married her for political reasons and then divorced her a few months later.

00:30:27.878 --> 00:30:39.047
Health problems In 1540, Henry was 49 and he had serious health problems.

00:30:39.107 --> 00:30:43.418
He was very fat and could not walk well.

00:30:43.478 --> 00:30:52.581
Soon after divorcing Anne of Cleves, he married a pretty girl of 19 years old, called Catherine Howard.

00:30:52.641 --> 00:30:59.359
But because she had relationships with other men, Henry accused her of treason.

00:30:59.419 --> 00:31:04.316
She was beheaded in 1542.

00:31:04.376 --> 00:31:14.728
The Last Queen Henry married his sixth and last queen in 1543.

00:31:14.788 --> 00:31:21.109
Her name was Catherine Parr, and she was a quiet, well-educated woman.

00:31:21.169 --> 00:31:26.918
She looked after Henry's three children, Mary, Elizabeth and Edward.

00:31:26.978 --> 00:31:31.327
She was kind to them and was interested in their education.

00:31:31.388 --> 00:31:34.099
Henry was happy with her.

00:31:34.159 --> 00:31:41.324
During Henry's last years, he could not walk and servants carried him everywhere.

00:31:41.384 --> 00:31:45.246
He also had very bad headaches.

00:31:45.306 --> 00:31:48.817
Catherine looked after him lovingly.

00:31:48.878 --> 00:31:54.571
Henry died on the 28th of January 1547 at the age of 55.

00:31:54.631 --> 00:32:04.738
He was buried at Windsor next to his favourite wife, Jane Seymour.

00:32:04.798 --> 00:32:16.938
Chapter 4 The Guildhall There were long steps from Westminster Palace to the River Thames.

00:32:16.999 --> 00:32:21.462
Soldiers stored on both sides of the steps.

00:32:21.522 --> 00:32:27.776
The people of London were near the river looking at the Royal Barge.

00:32:27.836 --> 00:32:36.310
When Tom came out, the crowd shouted, Long live Prince Edward!

00:32:36.370 --> 00:32:43.454
Tom wore beautiful white clothes and jewels for the important banquet.

00:32:43.514 --> 00:32:49.886
He looked at the river and thought about his friends and his games.

00:32:49.946 --> 00:32:57.651
He walked down the stairs to the royal barge and the lords and ladies bowed.

00:32:57.711 --> 00:33:05.334
Tom stood at the front of the barge as it moved slowly down the river to the Guildhall.

00:33:05.394 --> 00:33:11.266
He was excited because everything was new to him.

00:33:11.326 --> 00:33:21.978
The Guildhall was a big building near the river where all the rich and important men of London were waiting for the prince.

00:33:22.038 --> 00:33:30.261
At the same time John Canty took Edward and pulled him down, putting Lane.

00:33:30.322 --> 00:33:33.973
People laughed and followed them.

00:33:34.034 --> 00:33:37.756
Teach that boy a lesson!

00:33:37.817 --> 00:33:40.828
shouted a young woman.

00:33:40.888 --> 00:33:48.093
When they came near John Canty's house, Father Andrew stood in front of them.

00:33:48.153 --> 00:33:50.034
Don't hurt him!

00:33:50.094 --> 00:33:52.146
Let him go!

00:33:52.206 --> 00:33:54.990
Said Father Andrew.

00:33:55.050 --> 00:34:00.236
John Canty was angry and did not answer him.

00:34:00.296 --> 00:34:06.630
He hit Father Andrew on the head with a stick and he fell to the ground.

00:34:06.690 --> 00:34:10.562
John Canty pulled Edward home.

00:34:10.622 --> 00:34:20.029
He opened the door of his small room and said to his wife, Here is your dear son.

00:34:20.090 --> 00:34:25.826
He doesn't have a penny for us and he's mad too.

00:34:25.885 --> 00:34:33.412
Tom's mother ran to Edward and said, Oh my poor boy.

00:34:33.432 --> 00:34:37.884
No money, no food.

00:34:37.944 --> 00:34:44.229
Said John Canty to Edward and he pushed him to the floor.

00:34:44.288 --> 00:34:47.910
Tom's father was a cruel man.

00:34:47.970 --> 00:34:51.272
There was a voice outside the door.

00:34:51.332 --> 00:34:55.330
John Canty, quick, open the door.

00:34:55.390 --> 00:34:57.375
What's the matter?

00:34:57.435 --> 00:34:58.796
Said Canty.

00:34:58.856 --> 00:35:01.757
You hit Father Andrew on the head.

00:35:01.817 --> 00:35:04.598
And now he's dead.

00:35:04.658 --> 00:35:06.768
Said a young man.

00:35:06.828 --> 00:35:08.268
Dead?

00:35:08.328 --> 00:35:10.739
Asked John Canty.

00:35:10.799 --> 00:35:12.770
This is bad.

00:35:12.830 --> 00:35:17.111
A lot of people saw me when I hit the old man.

00:35:17.171 --> 00:35:22.216
He turned to his wife and said, quick.

00:35:22.276 --> 00:35:27.752
Take the girls and meet me at London Bridge.

00:35:27.812 --> 00:35:31.992
I'll take another road with the boy.

00:35:32.053 --> 00:35:42.135
Kanti took Edward by the arm and pulled him through the small, dark streets until they came to the river.

00:35:42.195 --> 00:35:45.886
There he saw a crowd of people.

00:35:45.946 --> 00:35:50.067
Some of them were sitting at tables and drinking.

00:35:50.128 --> 00:35:52.118
What's all this?

00:35:52.178 --> 00:35:54.549
County asked a man.

00:35:54.609 --> 00:35:57.110
What are you waiting for?

00:35:57.170 --> 00:35:59.222
Don't you know?

00:35:59.282 --> 00:36:00.812
Said the man.

00:36:00.872 --> 00:36:05.976
We're waiting to see Prince Edward in the Royal Barge.

00:36:06.036 --> 00:36:10.158
He's going to a banquet at the Guild Hall.

00:36:10.218 --> 00:36:13.630
Here, have a drink.

00:36:13.690 --> 00:36:18.141
He gave John County a big cup.

00:36:18.201 --> 00:36:24.122
Canty removed his hand from Edward's arm to pick up the cup.

00:36:24.182 --> 00:36:29.054
Edward quickly ran away between the men's legs.

00:36:29.114 --> 00:36:31.484
Canty looked down.

00:36:31.544 --> 00:36:33.565
Where's the boy?

00:36:33.625 --> 00:36:34.856
Stop in!

00:36:34.916 --> 00:36:36.666
Catch him!

00:36:36.726 --> 00:36:43.889
Edward ran away and thought, I must go to the guild hall and find Tom.

00:36:43.949 --> 00:36:47.515
Then we can change clothes again.

00:36:47.575 --> 00:36:54.884
When Tom came into the guild hall, everyone stood up and bowed.

00:36:54.944 --> 00:37:01.298
He sat at the high table with the prince's sisters and Lady Jane.

00:37:01.359 --> 00:37:06.682
Hundreds of servants brought in all kinds of food.

00:37:06.742 --> 00:37:14.136
There was a lot of meat, fish and cheese and many different cakes.

00:37:14.196 --> 00:37:17.352
Soon the banquet began.

00:37:17.412 --> 00:37:23.428
Everyone talked and laughed, and there were singers and dancers.

00:37:23.488 --> 00:37:31.524
Tom was surprised by everything he saw, and started to enjoy the royal banquet.

00:37:31.584 --> 00:37:38.192
Edward finally reached the guild hall, and he was tired and dirty.

00:37:38.252 --> 00:37:42.180
He went to one of the soldiers and cried.

00:37:42.240 --> 00:37:44.331
I'm Prince Edward.

00:37:44.391 --> 00:37:46.182
Open the doors.

00:37:46.242 --> 00:37:48.464
I want to come in.

00:37:48.524 --> 00:37:51.255
The soldier laughed at him.

00:37:51.315 --> 00:37:54.447
I order you to open the doors.

00:37:54.507 --> 00:37:55.708
He cried.

00:37:55.768 --> 00:37:57.558
Don't be a fool.

00:37:57.618 --> 00:37:59.430
Said the soldier.

00:37:59.490 --> 00:38:02.042
Stand back.

00:38:02.102 --> 00:38:06.365
The people in the crowd were angry.

00:38:06.425 --> 00:38:09.978
Send this boy away!

00:38:10.038 --> 00:38:11.528
They shouted.

00:38:11.588 --> 00:38:13.138
He's mad.

00:38:13.198 --> 00:38:17.909
We want to see the prince when the banquet finishes.

00:38:17.970 --> 00:38:20.630
Go away, boy!

00:38:20.690 --> 00:38:22.951
I won't go away.

00:38:23.011 --> 00:38:25.721
I am Prince Edward.

00:38:25.781 --> 00:38:29.552
The boy in there is a pauper.

00:38:29.612 --> 00:38:33.717
I am the son of King Henry.

00:38:33.778 --> 00:38:40.976
The crowd began to look dangerous, but Edward did not move.

00:38:41.036 --> 00:38:50.063
Then a tall man with black hair came out of the angry crowd and stood next to Edward.

00:38:50.124 --> 00:38:54.866
Perhaps you're a prince, and perhaps you're not.

00:38:54.926 --> 00:38:56.548
Said the man.

00:38:56.608 --> 00:39:02.582
But you're a courageous boy, and I like you, so I'll help you.

00:39:02.643 --> 00:39:04.698
Who are you, sir?

00:39:04.758 --> 00:39:06.354
asked Edward.

00:39:06.415 --> 00:39:12.251
My name is Miles Hendon, and I'm a soldier of the King of England.

00:39:12.311 --> 00:39:18.248
I returned from France yesterday, and I'm going to my home in the country.

00:39:18.308 --> 00:39:22.101
The dangerous crowd came nearer.

00:39:22.162 --> 00:39:23.784
Stand back!

00:39:23.844 --> 00:39:26.580
Cried miles to the crowd.

00:39:26.640 --> 00:39:30.446
He took out his sword and held it up.

00:39:30.506 --> 00:39:32.326
Kill them!

00:39:32.386 --> 00:39:36.270
Cried someone from the back of the crowd.

00:39:36.330 --> 00:39:40.062
People started to throw things at them.

00:39:40.122 --> 00:39:44.804
Miles stood in front of Edward and defended him.

00:39:44.864 --> 00:39:50.718
The crowd was big and angry and Miles was alone.

00:39:50.778 --> 00:39:55.972
Suddenly, everyone stopped shouting and fighting.

00:39:56.032 --> 00:40:02.245
They heard the sound of horses, and a soldier cried, Oh, stand back!

00:40:02.305 --> 00:40:05.446
The king's first lord is coming!

00:40:05.506 --> 00:40:08.998
The soldiers pushed the crowd back.

00:40:09.058 --> 00:40:14.800
Lord Hartford ran up the stairs and went into the guild hall.

00:40:14.860 --> 00:40:24.320
He went to Tom and said, Your Majesty, I'm sorry, your father is dead.

00:40:24.380 --> 00:40:31.490
Then he looked at the people and shouted, King Henry is dead.

00:40:31.550 --> 00:40:35.121
Long live King Edward.

00:40:35.182 --> 00:40:42.476
Everyone at the banquet shouted, Long live King Edward.

00:40:42.536 --> 00:40:49.902
Miles Hendon quickly took Edward's arm and they ran away.

00:40:49.962 --> 00:40:56.724
Chapter 5 Sir Miles.

00:40:56.784 --> 00:41:01.816
Miles took Edward to an inn near London Bridge.

00:41:01.876 --> 00:41:07.748
People in the streets shouted, King Henry is dead!

00:41:07.808 --> 00:41:11.229
Long live King Edward!

00:41:11.289 --> 00:41:18.141
Edward thought of his father and became very sad and started to cry.

00:41:18.201 --> 00:41:24.296
King Henry was a difficult man, but he was always kind to him.

00:41:24.356 --> 00:41:27.688
And now he was dead.

00:41:27.748 --> 00:41:30.759
Then they heard more shouts.

00:41:30.819 --> 00:41:34.590
Long live King Edward!

00:41:34.650 --> 00:41:38.521
So now I am King?

00:41:38.581 --> 00:41:41.901
He said with tears in his eyes.

00:41:41.961 --> 00:41:44.382
Prince or King?

00:41:44.442 --> 00:41:45.842
Said Miles.

00:41:45.902 --> 00:41:48.212
You can stay with me tonight.

00:41:48.272 --> 00:41:51.936
We'll eat some food and rest.

00:41:51.996 --> 00:41:55.752
Miles' room at the inn was small.

00:41:55.812 --> 00:42:02.005
There was a bed, two chairs, a table, and a wash stand.

00:42:02.066 --> 00:42:06.418
Edward was very tired and fell on the bed.

00:42:06.478 --> 00:42:09.110
Call me when the food is ready.

00:42:09.170 --> 00:42:10.750
He said.

00:42:10.810 --> 00:42:16.564
Miles saw that the boy was cold and covered him with his jacket.

00:42:16.624 --> 00:42:18.906
Yes, your majesty.

00:42:18.966 --> 00:42:21.464
Said Miles, smiling.

00:42:21.524 --> 00:42:24.652
Miles went to get some food.

00:42:24.712 --> 00:42:28.596
Your banquet is ready your majesty.

00:42:28.656 --> 00:42:33.428
Edward washed his hands and sat down at the table.

00:42:33.488 --> 00:42:36.090
Miles sat down too.

00:42:36.150 --> 00:42:37.370
Wait.

00:42:37.431 --> 00:42:38.842
Said Edward.

00:42:38.902 --> 00:42:40.462
Stand up.

00:42:40.522 --> 00:42:42.514
I am your king.

00:42:42.574 --> 00:42:45.556
You must wait for my orders.

00:42:45.616 --> 00:42:48.308
Miles stood up.

00:42:48.368 --> 00:42:51.392
Now you can sit down.

00:42:51.453 --> 00:42:55.338
They were both hungry and started to eat.

00:42:55.399 --> 00:43:05.866
After dinner, Edward looked at Myles and said, You are a courageous soldier of the king and you are good to me.

00:43:05.926 --> 00:43:10.900
Give me your sword and go down on your knee.

00:43:10.960 --> 00:43:16.345
With the side of the sword, Edward touched Myles on the shoulder.

00:43:16.405 --> 00:43:20.172
Stand up, sir, Myles Hendon.

00:43:20.232 --> 00:43:23.958
Now, you are one of my men.

00:43:24.018 --> 00:43:28.340
Miles stood up and laughed.

00:43:28.400 --> 00:43:35.734
Edward fell asleep with his head on the table, and Miles took him to bed.

00:43:35.794 --> 00:43:37.425
Poor boy.

00:43:37.445 --> 00:43:43.608
He said, perhaps he'll be well again after a long sleep.

00:43:43.668 --> 00:43:48.200
That night, Miles slept on the floor.

00:43:48.260 --> 00:43:53.494
The next morning, Miles looked at the boy sleeping on the bed.

00:43:53.554 --> 00:43:55.484
The poor boy.

00:43:55.544 --> 00:43:56.896
He thought.

00:43:56.956 --> 00:44:05.082
He can sleep another hour, and I'll go out to the market and buy him some new clothes.

00:44:05.142 --> 00:44:11.116
In the streets of London, everyone was talking about the new king.

00:44:11.176 --> 00:44:14.374
Miles listened to them.

00:44:14.434 --> 00:44:20.283
People say the new king is mad.

00:44:20.343 --> 00:44:22.914
Said an old woman.

00:44:22.974 --> 00:44:26.406
He doesn't want to be king.

00:44:26.426 --> 00:44:30.428
He says he's a pooper.

00:44:30.488 --> 00:44:31.758
Yes.

00:44:31.818 --> 00:44:34.949
He says it's all a mistake.

00:44:35.009 --> 00:44:36.670
Said a young man.

00:44:36.690 --> 00:44:40.722
The poor young king is mad.

00:44:40.782 --> 00:44:43.645
Completely mad.

00:44:43.706 --> 00:44:47.089
Said another man laughing.

00:44:47.149 --> 00:44:50.100
Miles started thinking.

00:44:50.160 --> 00:44:54.962
Perhaps Edward is telling me the truth.

00:44:55.022 --> 00:44:58.612
Perhaps he is the King of England.

00:44:58.672 --> 00:45:03.494
He went back to the inn with the new clothes.

00:45:03.554 --> 00:45:09.226
When he got back to his room, he was very surprised.

00:45:09.286 --> 00:45:12.451
Edward was gone.

00:45:12.511 --> 00:45:18.899
Miles immediately went to the man at the inn and asked.

00:45:18.959 --> 00:45:21.180
Where is the young boy?

00:45:21.200 --> 00:45:24.883
Oh, dear, said the man.

00:45:24.943 --> 00:45:27.405
Please don't get angry, sir.

00:45:27.465 --> 00:45:29.836
Well, where is he?

00:45:29.897 --> 00:45:32.888
Asked Miles angrily.

00:45:32.948 --> 00:45:35.690
Answer my question.

00:45:35.750 --> 00:45:39.354
The man's face became red.

00:45:39.414 --> 00:45:44.179
When you were away a man came and took the boy with him.

00:45:44.199 --> 00:45:45.882
A man?

00:45:45.942 --> 00:45:47.303
Said Miles.

00:45:47.363 --> 00:45:49.035
Surprised?

00:45:49.095 --> 00:45:51.097
Oh no.

00:45:51.157 --> 00:45:53.390
It was probably his father.

00:45:53.410 --> 00:45:55.642
The poor boy.

00:45:55.703 --> 00:45:57.602
Where did they go?

00:45:57.662 --> 00:46:01.501
Well sir, they went towards Sothek.

00:46:01.561 --> 00:46:03.042
Said the man.

00:46:03.102 --> 00:46:06.673
And they disappeared in the crowd.

00:46:06.733 --> 00:46:08.544
Poor Edward.

00:46:08.604 --> 00:46:10.324
Said Miles.

00:46:10.384 --> 00:46:13.266
I must find him.

00:46:13.326 --> 00:46:21.828
He ran out of the inn and went towards Sothek, looking for his young friend.

00:46:21.888 --> 00:46:32.352
At the same time, Edward had to follow John Canty through a forest outside London to an old barn.

00:46:32.413 --> 00:46:39.426
Inside the barn, there were many beggars, thieves and vagabonds.

00:46:39.486 --> 00:46:43.188
John Canty knew most of them.

00:46:43.248 --> 00:46:46.380
What strange people!

00:46:46.440 --> 00:46:50.912
Thought Edward, looking at them silently.

00:46:50.972 --> 00:46:53.580
Where do they come from?

00:46:53.640 --> 00:46:57.138
Who's this boy, John?

00:46:57.198 --> 00:47:02.049
Asked an old beggar with dirty clothes.

00:47:02.109 --> 00:47:04.890
He's my son.

00:47:04.950 --> 00:47:06.950
Said John Canty.

00:47:07.010 --> 00:47:08.050
No.

00:47:08.110 --> 00:47:09.751
Cried Edward.

00:47:09.811 --> 00:47:11.561
I'm not his son.

00:47:11.621 --> 00:47:14.482
I'm the king of England.

00:47:14.542 --> 00:47:20.061
Everyone in the barn started to laugh.

00:47:20.121 --> 00:47:30.556
An old beggar with long hair and no teeth said, The King of England.

00:47:30.616 --> 00:47:34.610
He's the king of phones.

00:47:34.670 --> 00:47:37.524
And everyone laughed again.

00:47:37.584 --> 00:47:42.044
Edward was very sad.

00:47:42.104 --> 00:47:51.876
Soon, everyone was saying unkind things to him, and he wanted to cry.

00:47:51.936 --> 00:47:53.626
But he didn't.

00:47:53.686 --> 00:48:00.468
He went to sit in a corner and thought, Will Miles find me here?

00:48:00.528 --> 00:48:06.520
He was tired and hungry, and he soon fell asleep.

00:48:06.580 --> 00:48:13.646
When Edward woke up the next morning, everyone in the barn was sleeping.

00:48:13.706 --> 00:48:22.153
He quickly and quietly opened the door and ran away into the forest.

00:48:22.213 --> 00:48:28.715
He ran all the way to the first village and stopped at the market.

00:48:28.775 --> 00:48:31.736
Suddenly he heard a voice.

00:48:31.796 --> 00:48:33.466
Edward.

00:48:33.526 --> 00:48:37.247
He turned around and saw miles.

00:48:37.307 --> 00:48:40.618
Oh, how happy I am to see you.

00:48:40.678 --> 00:48:43.560
Said Edward, smiling.

00:48:43.620 --> 00:48:46.592
I looked for you everywhere.

00:48:46.652 --> 00:48:48.533
Said Miles.

00:48:48.593 --> 00:48:52.584
Edward told him about John Canty.

00:48:52.644 --> 00:48:58.677
And Miles told him what he heard at the market the day before.

00:48:58.737 --> 00:49:00.518
I believe you.

00:49:00.578 --> 00:49:04.700
And now I know you're the king, your majesty.

00:49:04.760 --> 00:49:06.560
Said Miles.

00:49:06.620 --> 00:49:10.965
Let's go to my home, Hendon Hall.

00:49:11.025 --> 00:49:21.125
It's not far from Westminster Palace, and we can think of a plan to help you get back into the palace.

00:49:21.185 --> 00:49:24.627
I'm glad you believed me, Sir Miles.

00:49:24.688 --> 00:49:28.029
Said Edward.

00:49:28.090 --> 00:49:44.360
Chapter 6 The Life of a King It was morning, and Tom woke up in a big, beautiful bed in Westminster Palace.

00:49:44.420 --> 00:49:51.601
When he opened his eyes, he saw two gentlemen by the side of his bed.

00:49:51.662 --> 00:49:54.002
Your Majesty.

00:49:54.062 --> 00:49:56.643
Said the first gentleman.

00:49:56.703 --> 00:50:00.374
It's eight o'clock, Your Majesty.

00:50:00.434 --> 00:50:03.606
Said the second gentleman.

00:50:03.666 --> 00:50:05.548
What?

00:50:05.608 --> 00:50:07.109
said Tom.

00:50:07.169 --> 00:50:10.362
Does your Majesty wish to rise?

00:50:10.422 --> 00:50:13.384
Ask the first gentleman.

00:50:13.444 --> 00:50:15.586
Do you mean?

00:50:15.646 --> 00:50:18.258
Do I want to get up?

00:50:18.318 --> 00:50:20.860
Yes, your Majesty.

00:50:20.920 --> 00:50:23.641
Yes, I do.

00:50:23.702 --> 00:50:25.522
Said Tom.

00:50:25.582 --> 00:50:29.223
Where are my clothes?

00:50:29.283 --> 00:50:37.367
One gentleman brought Tom's underclothes into the room and gave them to a second gentleman.

00:50:37.427 --> 00:50:41.460
And the second gentleman gave them to a third gentleman.

00:50:41.520 --> 00:50:47.096
And the third gentleman helped Tom get into his underclothes.

00:50:47.156 --> 00:50:53.390
In this way the gentleman dressed Tom in his expensive clothes.

00:50:53.450 --> 00:50:57.098
An hour later he was ready.

00:50:57.158 --> 00:51:02.674
Tom went to another beautiful room to have breakfast.

00:51:02.734 --> 00:51:06.946
One servant brought the food into the room.

00:51:07.007 --> 00:51:10.248
He gave it to a second servant.

00:51:10.308 --> 00:51:18.470
The second servant gave it to a third servant and the third servant put it on the table.

00:51:18.530 --> 00:51:23.232
A fourth servant put some food on Tom's plate.

00:51:23.292 --> 00:51:29.113
Two other servants stood behind Tom's chair and did nothing.

00:51:29.173 --> 00:51:33.234
The servants did everything for Tom.

00:51:33.294 --> 00:51:42.555
After breakfast, a servant said, Your Majesty, Lord Hartford wants to speak to you.

00:51:42.615 --> 00:51:46.506
Lord Hartford came in and bowed.

00:51:46.566 --> 00:51:48.896
Is your Majesty ready?

00:51:48.956 --> 00:51:53.038
The men are waiting in the council chamber.

00:51:53.098 --> 00:51:59.922
Tom went to the council chamber and sat in the king's gold chair.

00:51:59.982 --> 00:52:08.106
Men came, bowed and kissed his hand and read from long pieces of paper.

00:52:08.167 --> 00:52:13.590
It was very boring and it went on for hours.

00:52:13.650 --> 00:52:17.176
One man talked about money.

00:52:17.236 --> 00:52:25.354
There is no money, your Majesty, because King Henry spent all of it.

00:52:25.414 --> 00:52:35.900
He built a lot of castles and wore expensive clothes and jewels, and his funeral was very expensive, too.

00:52:35.960 --> 00:52:41.324
You have one thousand servants, and you must pay them.

00:52:41.384 --> 00:52:51.972
Tom looked at the man and said, We can live in a small house with only ten servants.

00:52:52.032 --> 00:52:58.336
There is a nice house in the city near Pudding Lane.

00:52:58.396 --> 00:53:05.460
Lord Hertford took Tom's arm gently and Tom stopped talking.

00:53:05.520 --> 00:53:08.772
Tom's face was red.

00:53:08.832 --> 00:53:12.375
Oh, when will this end?

00:53:12.435 --> 00:53:14.210
He thought.

00:53:14.270 --> 00:53:20.118
I want to play ball or swim in the river."

00:53:20.178 --> 00:53:27.352
He had lunch in the Great Dining Room and the food was delicious.

00:53:27.412 --> 00:53:34.558
But he could not stop thinking about his friends and games at the river.

00:53:34.618 --> 00:53:42.519
After lunch, Tom went back to Prince Edward's room and sent everyone away.

00:53:42.579 --> 00:53:48.398
After a few minutes, a boy came in quietly.

00:53:48.458 --> 00:53:50.940
Who are you?

00:53:51.000 --> 00:53:52.710
asked Tom.

00:53:52.770 --> 00:53:56.832
Oh, your Majesty is really ill.

00:53:56.892 --> 00:53:58.382
Said the boy.

00:53:58.442 --> 00:54:00.544
I'm Humphrey Marlow.

00:54:00.604 --> 00:54:02.924
I'm your whipping boy.

00:54:02.984 --> 00:54:05.846
My whipping boy?

00:54:05.906 --> 00:54:07.416
cried Tom.

00:54:07.476 --> 00:54:09.578
Yes, your Majesty.

00:54:09.638 --> 00:54:11.273
Said the boy.

00:54:11.333 --> 00:54:18.709
When you make mistakes during your Greek lesson, your teacher gets angry.

00:54:18.769 --> 00:54:25.290
But no one hits the Prince of Wales, so he hits me.

00:54:25.350 --> 00:54:27.401
That's my job.

00:54:27.461 --> 00:54:33.742
But now you're king and perhaps you won't study Greek anymore.

00:54:33.802 --> 00:54:39.484
Then I'll lose my job and my family will be hungry.

00:54:39.544 --> 00:54:41.776
We'll live on the streets.

00:54:41.836 --> 00:54:43.176
What?

00:54:43.236 --> 00:54:47.880
Tom looked at the boy and laughed loudly.

00:54:47.940 --> 00:54:50.320
Listen Humphrey.

00:54:50.380 --> 00:54:55.864
I won't stop my studies and I'll make a lot of mistakes.

00:54:55.924 --> 00:55:02.117
They'll pay you more than before and you can work all your life.

00:55:02.177 --> 00:55:05.259
Oh, thank you Your Majesty.

00:55:05.319 --> 00:55:08.190
You're very kind.

00:55:08.250 --> 00:55:16.025
Tom liked talking to Humphrey and learned a lot of things about Edward's life.

00:55:16.085 --> 00:55:22.480
Lord Hartford came for Tom and took him back to the council chamber.

00:55:22.540 --> 00:55:25.694
You're feeling better, Your Majesty.

00:55:25.754 --> 00:55:27.375
I can see it.

00:55:27.435 --> 00:55:29.516
You remember more.

00:55:29.576 --> 00:55:31.818
Said Lord Hartford.

00:55:31.879 --> 00:55:36.736
Do you remember where the great seal is?

00:55:36.796 --> 00:55:39.490
The great seal?

00:55:39.551 --> 00:55:41.242
asked Tom.

00:55:41.302 --> 00:55:43.722
What's it like?

00:55:43.783 --> 00:55:45.714
Oh, dear.

00:55:45.774 --> 00:55:47.416
Thought the Lord.

00:55:47.476 --> 00:55:50.748
He's still not well.

00:55:50.808 --> 00:56:01.034
When they reached the council chamber, Tom had to sign Edward's name on a lot of papers all afternoon.

00:56:01.094 --> 00:56:04.522
The king's job was not easy.

00:56:04.582 --> 00:56:08.750
It was a long, boring afternoon.

00:56:08.810 --> 00:56:13.053
In the evening, there was another royal dinner.

00:56:13.112 --> 00:56:18.375
And after that, Tom finally went to bed.

00:56:18.436 --> 00:56:22.768
My clothes are beautiful.

00:56:22.828 --> 00:56:28.680
And the palace is splendid, he thought.

00:56:28.741 --> 00:56:32.450
The food is delicious.

00:56:32.510 --> 00:56:36.801
And now I'm never hungry.

00:56:36.861 --> 00:56:41.514
But I don't want to be king.

00:56:41.574 --> 00:56:44.207
Every day is the same.

00:56:44.227 --> 00:56:50.092
Putting lane is more fun.

00:56:50.152 --> 00:56:54.905
Listening activity.

00:56:54.965 --> 00:56:58.308
Hello Humphrey.

00:56:58.368 --> 00:57:01.746
I'm Tom Canty.

00:57:01.806 --> 00:57:04.603
Where do you live?

00:57:04.664 --> 00:57:06.844
Hello, Tom.

00:57:06.904 --> 00:57:11.798
I live in a small house near the church.

00:57:11.858 --> 00:57:15.250
It's far from the palace.

00:57:15.310 --> 00:57:22.764
What time do you get up in the morning to come to work?

00:57:22.784 --> 00:57:29.708
I get up at half past six and have breakfast at seven.

00:57:29.768 --> 00:57:33.008
Then I come to work.

00:57:33.069 --> 00:57:38.070
How many brothers and sisters have you got?

00:57:38.130 --> 00:57:43.512
I've got two brothers and three sisters.

00:57:43.572 --> 00:57:50.776
My brother James works at the Baker shop in Pudding Lane.

00:57:50.836 --> 00:57:54.318
What do you do in your free time?

00:57:54.338 --> 00:58:04.344
I don't have much free time, but on Sundays I like playing ball.

00:58:04.404 --> 00:58:16.950
Chapter 7 Hendon Hall The next day Edward rode with miles on his horse.

00:58:17.010 --> 00:58:22.132
In the afternoon they came to a high hill.

00:58:22.192 --> 00:58:30.998
Miles stopped and said, Look, that's my home, among the trees.

00:58:31.058 --> 00:58:37.738
It's a very big house with 50 rooms and 20 servants.

00:58:37.798 --> 00:58:43.882
They rode down the hill and passed through a big gate.

00:58:43.942 --> 00:58:47.315
This is Hendon Hall.

00:58:47.376 --> 00:58:50.118
Said Miles happily.

00:58:50.178 --> 00:58:53.050
How glad I am to be home.

00:58:53.110 --> 00:58:56.954
My family will be so happy to see me.

00:58:57.014 --> 00:59:02.600
Miles ran into the house and Edward followed him.

00:59:02.660 --> 00:59:08.605
There was a young man with blonde hair at a long table.

00:59:08.666 --> 00:59:10.006
Hew!

00:59:10.066 --> 00:59:12.228
Cried Miles.

00:59:12.288 --> 00:59:16.152
Aren't you happy to see me?

00:59:16.212 --> 00:59:18.624
Where's Father?

00:59:18.684 --> 00:59:26.083
The young man was unfriendly and looked at him with cold eyes.

00:59:26.144 --> 00:59:28.688
Who are you?

00:59:28.748 --> 00:59:30.678
Don't you know me?

00:59:30.698 --> 00:59:34.569
I'm your brother, Miles.

00:59:34.629 --> 00:59:38.430
I'm back from France after the war.

00:59:38.490 --> 00:59:42.121
My brother died in France.

00:59:42.181 --> 00:59:43.721
Said Hugh?

00:59:43.781 --> 00:59:47.002
We received a letter from his friend.

00:59:47.062 --> 00:59:48.242
No, no.

00:59:48.262 --> 00:59:50.193
I'm here.

00:59:50.253 --> 00:59:51.983
Said Miles.

00:59:52.043 --> 00:59:54.184
Where's my father?

00:59:54.244 --> 00:59:56.050
He'll know me.

00:59:56.110 --> 00:59:57.846
He's dead.

00:59:57.906 --> 00:59:59.366
Said Hugh.

00:59:59.426 --> 01:00:00.656
No.

01:00:00.716 --> 01:00:02.517
Poor Father.

01:00:02.577 --> 01:00:04.397
Cried Miles.

01:00:04.457 --> 01:00:07.478
Then call the servants.

01:00:07.538 --> 01:00:09.369
They'll know me.

01:00:09.429 --> 01:00:12.390
All the servants are new.

01:00:12.450 --> 01:00:13.950
Said Hugh.

01:00:14.010 --> 01:00:16.421
You sent them away.

01:00:16.481 --> 01:00:19.222
Cried Miles angrily.

01:00:19.282 --> 01:00:22.156
Now I understand.

01:00:22.216 --> 01:00:28.390
You wrote the letter because you wanted the house and the money.

01:00:28.450 --> 01:00:34.712
But your plan won't work because Lady Edith will remember me.

01:00:34.772 --> 01:00:40.755
Lady Edith knows that Miles Hendon is dead.

01:00:40.815 --> 01:00:42.536
Said you.

01:00:42.596 --> 01:00:46.337
She's my wife now.

01:00:46.397 --> 01:00:51.622
Miles was furious and ran across the room.

01:00:51.683 --> 01:00:54.798
You took my home and my land.

01:00:54.858 --> 01:00:56.860
You took my money.

01:00:56.920 --> 01:01:00.732
And you also took the woman I love.

01:01:00.792 --> 01:01:02.934
I'll kill you."

01:01:02.995 --> 01:01:08.999
He took Hugh by the shirt and pushed him against the wall angrily.

01:01:09.019 --> 01:01:09.980
Help!

01:01:10.040 --> 01:01:11.151
Help!

01:01:11.211 --> 01:01:12.712
Help!

01:01:12.772 --> 01:01:14.744
Shouted Hugh.

01:01:14.804 --> 01:01:20.320
The servants ran into the room and pulled miles from him.

01:01:20.380 --> 01:01:24.706
They took Miles and Edward away to prison.

01:01:24.766 --> 01:01:28.268
The prison was a terrible place.

01:01:28.328 --> 01:01:32.682
It was dark, cold and crowded.

01:01:32.742 --> 01:01:36.063
There were rats everywhere.

01:01:36.124 --> 01:01:42.288
Miles and Edward were chained together in a large noisy room.

01:01:42.348 --> 01:01:47.594
Some prisoners sang and others fought and shouted.

01:01:47.654 --> 01:01:52.228
A man hit a woman and almost killed her.

01:01:52.288 --> 01:01:55.490
Her face was covered with blood.

01:01:55.550 --> 01:01:58.822
Another woman cried loudly.

01:01:58.882 --> 01:02:01.072
What is the matter?

01:02:01.132 --> 01:02:03.824
Edward asked the woman.

01:02:03.884 --> 01:02:13.047
Tomorrow, the soldiers are going to hang me because I stole some cheese.

01:02:13.107 --> 01:02:15.757
She said, crying.

01:02:15.817 --> 01:02:19.828
Another sad young man spoke to Miles.

01:02:19.888 --> 01:02:25.712
They're going to hang me, because I killed a deer in the King's Park.

01:02:25.772 --> 01:02:28.454
But it's not true!

01:02:28.514 --> 01:02:32.066
Then he started to cry.

01:02:32.126 --> 01:02:37.290
Oh, prisons are sad, ugly place.

01:02:37.350 --> 01:02:38.971
Said Edward.

01:02:39.031 --> 01:02:42.530
No one helps these poor people.

01:02:42.590 --> 01:02:47.720
One day, I will change these cruel laws.

01:02:47.781 --> 01:02:51.152
No one slept that night.

01:02:51.212 --> 01:02:56.834
The next day, Miles and Edward were in front of the judge.

01:02:56.894 --> 01:03:00.576
Why are this man and this boy here?

01:03:00.636 --> 01:03:02.606
Asked the judge.

01:03:02.667 --> 01:03:06.739
Miles wanted to speak, but the judge said...

01:03:06.799 --> 01:03:08.200
Be quiet.

01:03:08.261 --> 01:03:11.524
He turned to Hugh and asked.

01:03:11.584 --> 01:03:15.536
Why did you bring them here, Mr. Hendon?

01:03:15.596 --> 01:03:19.489
Hugh explained his story to the judge.

01:03:19.549 --> 01:03:22.071
Then Miles tried to speak.

01:03:22.131 --> 01:03:25.223
But the judge did not listen to him.

01:03:25.283 --> 01:03:29.586
The man must sit in the stalks for two hours.

01:03:29.646 --> 01:03:30.997
Said the judge.

01:03:31.057 --> 01:03:34.640
Then he and the boy can leave.

01:03:34.700 --> 01:03:37.898
Take them away immediately.

01:03:37.958 --> 01:03:40.436
cried Edward.

01:03:40.496 --> 01:03:42.786
He's my servant!

01:03:42.846 --> 01:03:45.737
You don't know what you're doing!

01:03:45.797 --> 01:03:51.188
Be quiet, boy, or the soldiers will hit you."

01:03:51.248 --> 01:03:53.179
said the judge.

01:03:53.239 --> 01:03:57.460
The soldiers put miles into the stalks.

01:03:57.520 --> 01:04:04.118
Some people stopped and looked, and others threw bad eggs at him.

01:04:04.178 --> 01:04:09.284
Edward stood in front of Miles and tried to protect him.

01:04:09.344 --> 01:04:18.608
The people laughed and said, He's a courageous boy and he loves his friend.

01:04:18.668 --> 01:04:27.011
At the end of the two hours, the soldiers took Miles out of the stalks and he was free.

01:04:27.071 --> 01:04:36.577
He looked at Edward and said, Now we can finally go to London.

01:04:36.637 --> 01:04:50.568
Chapter 8 The New King When Miles and Edward arrived in London, they saw a crowd of people in the streets.

01:04:50.628 --> 01:04:57.802
There were flags on all of the buildings, and a lot of noise everywhere.

01:04:57.862 --> 01:05:05.487
It was the 19th of February, and the next day was Coronation Day.

01:05:05.548 --> 01:05:10.230
Everyone was happy and excited.

01:05:10.290 --> 01:05:17.373
Miles and Edward were in the big crowd and they soon got lost.

01:05:17.433 --> 01:05:21.254
They could not find each other anymore.

01:05:21.314 --> 01:05:27.197
Poor Edward was cold, hungry and alone.

01:05:27.257 --> 01:05:37.432
Tom, on the other hand, was beginning to enjoy the royal palace, the beautiful new clothes, and the good food.

01:05:37.493 --> 01:05:43.767
Everyone bowed to him and listened to him, and he liked this.

01:05:43.827 --> 01:05:52.234
During his first days at the palace, he thought about his mother, sisters, and Edward.

01:05:52.294 --> 01:06:01.962
But, as the days passed, he almost forgot about them, because he liked his wonderful new life.

01:06:02.022 --> 01:06:05.954
He was happy and comfortable.

01:06:06.014 --> 01:06:12.038
The next morning was the 20th of February, coronation day.

01:06:12.098 --> 01:06:20.583
Tom thought, today I'm going to become King of England.

01:06:20.644 --> 01:06:27.580
I'm going to wear splendid new clothes and jewels in the parade.

01:06:27.640 --> 01:06:32.164
Oh, this is wonderful!

01:06:32.224 --> 01:06:41.822
Soon Tom Canty was splendidly dressed and riding a tall horse in the royal parade.

01:06:41.882 --> 01:06:49.316
Behind him there were lords and rich gentlemen dressed in their best clothes.

01:06:49.376 --> 01:06:56.285
There was music in the air, and thousands of happy people in the streets of London.

01:06:56.305 --> 01:07:01.457
Hurray for the new King of England!

01:07:01.517 --> 01:07:03.388
They shouted.

01:07:03.448 --> 01:07:09.180
Tom smiled, and often threw new coins to the people.

01:07:09.240 --> 01:07:12.592
He felt important.

01:07:12.652 --> 01:07:24.424
Suddenly, he saw his mother in the big crowd, She touched his leg and cried, Oh, my dear child!

01:07:24.484 --> 01:07:27.755
A soldier pushed her away.

01:07:27.816 --> 01:07:35.390
Tom looked at her and said, I don't know you, woman!

01:07:35.450 --> 01:07:41.324
His mother was very sad and disappeared in the crowd.

01:07:41.384 --> 01:07:47.532
After a moment, Tom thought, Oh no!

01:07:47.592 --> 01:07:50.699
What did I say?

01:07:50.759 --> 01:07:57.794
He felt terrible, and suddenly he was unhappy.

01:07:57.854 --> 01:08:04.998
The royal parade continued down the streets of London to Westminster Abbey.

01:08:05.058 --> 01:08:12.295
The church was full of people and beautifully decorated for the great day.

01:08:12.355 --> 01:08:22.283
At last, the archbishop of Canterbury took the crown of England and lifted it over Tom's head.

01:08:22.342 --> 01:08:25.614
Everyone was silent.

01:08:25.674 --> 01:08:35.290
Suddenly, a young boy with no shoes and old dirty clothes ran into the church.

01:08:35.350 --> 01:08:37.411
You're not the king!

01:08:37.431 --> 01:08:39.922
I'm the king!

01:08:39.982 --> 01:08:41.626
He cried.

01:08:41.686 --> 01:08:47.031
Everyone was surprised, and the people looked at each other.

01:08:47.091 --> 01:08:49.182
What's happening?

01:08:49.242 --> 01:08:51.714
Asked one gentleman.

01:08:51.774 --> 01:08:54.194
Who's that pauper?

01:08:54.254 --> 01:08:56.376
What does he want?

01:08:56.435 --> 01:08:58.646
Asked a lady.

01:08:58.706 --> 01:09:04.539
Lord Hertford quickly said, Soldiers, stop this boy.

01:09:04.599 --> 01:09:09.428
Edward and Tom looked at each other for a moment.

01:09:09.488 --> 01:09:12.878
No, said Tom.

01:09:12.938 --> 01:09:15.120
Don't touch him.

01:09:15.180 --> 01:09:18.643
He is the real king.

01:09:18.703 --> 01:09:21.796
Everyone was confused.

01:09:21.855 --> 01:09:28.450
Lord Hartford looked at the two boys and said, Look at their faces.

01:09:28.511 --> 01:09:31.102
They're identical.

01:09:31.163 --> 01:09:34.629
But who is our king?

01:09:34.689 --> 01:09:41.635
He is the real king, said Tom, smiling at Edward.

01:09:41.695 --> 01:09:45.456
Ask him about the great seal.

01:09:45.516 --> 01:09:49.327
Very well, said Lord Hartford.

01:09:49.388 --> 01:09:53.889
Only the real king can answer this question.

01:09:53.949 --> 01:09:57.190
Where's the great seal?

01:09:57.250 --> 01:10:05.754
Edward immediately said, Look inside the old Italian suit of armour in my room.

01:10:05.814 --> 01:10:08.854
The great seal's there.

01:10:08.914 --> 01:10:16.286
Lord Hartford sent Lord John to look for the great seal in the palace.

01:10:16.346 --> 01:10:22.367
When he returned, he said, I found the great seal.

01:10:22.427 --> 01:10:23.897
Here it is.

01:10:23.957 --> 01:10:26.588
The pauper is right.

01:10:26.648 --> 01:10:29.312
He is the king.

01:10:29.372 --> 01:10:37.424
The archbishop of Canterbury put the crown of England on Edward's young head.

01:10:37.484 --> 01:10:41.918
Everyone in the church stood up and cheered.

01:10:41.978 --> 01:10:46.362
Long live young King Edward!

01:10:46.421 --> 01:10:54.424
Tom looked at the great seal and said, I used it to crack nuts.

01:10:54.484 --> 01:10:57.974
I didn't know it was the great seal.

01:10:58.034 --> 01:11:04.386
He used a great seal of England to crack nuts.

01:11:04.446 --> 01:11:08.066
Said Lord Hartford loudly.

01:11:08.126 --> 01:11:11.726
How funny!

01:11:11.786 --> 01:11:18.370
All the great lords laughed and laughed.

01:11:18.430 --> 01:11:26.095
The great ceremony ended, and Edward became King Edward VI.

01:11:26.155 --> 01:11:32.837
The next day, Miles went to see his friend, King Edward VI.

01:11:32.897 --> 01:11:42.170
The young king was happy to see Sir Miles, who told him more about his problems with his brother Hugh.

01:11:42.230 --> 01:11:46.092
You were kind and helped me Sir Miles.

01:11:46.152 --> 01:11:48.234
said the young king.

01:11:48.294 --> 01:11:51.044
Now I will help you.

01:11:51.104 --> 01:11:56.476
You can go back to Hendon House because it's yours again.

01:11:56.536 --> 01:12:01.978
Your brother Hugh will give everything back to you.

01:12:02.038 --> 01:12:04.310
Thank you, King Edward.

01:12:04.370 --> 01:12:08.030
Said Sir Miles, happily.

01:12:08.090 --> 01:12:14.025
King Edward VI was a very good and kind king.

01:12:14.085 --> 01:12:18.288
because for those few days he was a pauper.

01:12:18.348 --> 01:12:24.310
He knew his people and understood their problems.

01:12:24.370 --> 01:12:31.704
Tom Canty was the king's best friend and lived in Westminster Palace.

01:12:31.764 --> 01:12:39.156
King Edward gave Tom's mother and sisters a lovely house in the country.

01:12:39.216 --> 01:12:44.245
And no one saw John Canty again.

01:12:44.305 --> 01:12:49.943
King Edward VI died when he was only 16.

01:12:50.003 --> 01:12:55.514
Tom was very sad and left Westminster Palace.

01:12:55.574 --> 01:13:00.905
He went to live with his mother and sisters in the country.

01:13:00.965 --> 01:13:11.967
Everyone remembered the young king for a long time because he loved all of his people, the rich and the poor.

